course: dictionary
lesson: 11969
title: Cater: food, needs and pleasing people
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word cater has three meanings, and the words around it tell you which one is used. «Mum will cater the party for thirty guests.» Here cater means to provide the food and drinks for an event, such as a party or wedding.
explain: «The holiday club caters for children aged 5 to 12.» Cater for means to provide what a group of people needs or wants. The clue is the group: the club is thinking about the needs of children of those ages.
explain: «The waiter kept catering to the fussy man, bringing him anything he asked for.» Cater to means to try too hard to please someone. The clue is the words kept and anything: the waiter goes too far to keep the man happy. Check your meaning by putting it in the sentence in place of the hard word.
fact: «Cater» means to provide food and drinks for an event.
fact: «Cater for» means to provide what a group of people needs or wants.
fact: «Cater to» means to try too hard to please someone.
fact: A «caterer» is a person or company whose job is to provide food for events.
fact: «Self-catering» means you cook for yourself, for example in a holiday flat.
exercise: «Mum will cater the party for thirty guests.» What does cater mean here? | To clean the house before the guests arrive | *To provide food and drinks for the party | To dance all night | To send out the invitations
exercise: «The holiday club caters for children aged 5 to 12.» What does cater for mean? | *To provide what children of that age need | To teach the children how to cook | To shout at the children until they are quiet | To cook all the food for the children
exercise: Find the word for the person whose job is to provide food for parties. | Guest | Cutlery | Cupboard | *Caterer
test: «The waiter kept catering to the fussy man, bringing him anything he asked for.» What does cater to mean here? | To write down his order on a pad | *To try too hard to please someone | To ignore him completely | To cook food for the whole street
test: «We are going self-catering this summer, so we will cook all our own meals.» What does self-catering mean? | To wash the dishes after a big party | *To cook for yourself | To be served by a waiter at a hotel | To eat at a different restaurant every day
exam: «The café caters for vegans as well as meat-eaters.» What does caters for mean? | To cook food for a wedding | To dislike vegan food | *To provide what the group needs or wants | To serve only meat to the meat-eaters
